  "verdict": {
    "ko": "이 실제 궤도 데이터(ISS/CSS 정거장 그룹, 24시간 창)에서, 도킹·결합된 물체(예: ISS와 도킹된 Progress·Cygnus·Crew Dragon)는 서로 완전히 동일한 TLE를 공유해 미스거리가 정확히 0km로 나온다. co-orbital 필터를 끄면 이 31쌍의 '가짜 충돌'이 임계값 15km 미만 구간의 경보를 전부 차지해 실제로 가장 가까운 진짜 근접 접근(57.5km, KNACKSAT-2/UITMSAT-2)이 경보 목록에 아예 안 보이게 된다. 필터를 켜면 이 노이즈가 사라지고 진짜 conjunction만 남는다. 단일 위험 숫자가 아니라 근거를 남기는 이유가 여기 있다.",
    "en": "In this real orbital data (the ISS/CSS station group, 24-hour window), docked/bolted-together objects (e.g. Progress, Cygnus, and Crew Dragon docked to the ISS) publish identical element sets and so report exactly 0 km miss distance. With the co-orbital filter off, those 31 'phantom collisions' fill every alert slot under about 15 km, burying the closest genuine conjunction (57.5 km, KNACKSAT-2/UITMSAT-2) off the list entirely. Turning the filter on removes that noise and leaves only real conjunctions, which is exactly why this system reports evidence, not a single risk number."
  },
  "provenance": {
    "backend": "sgp4 (python package v2.27) propagating a live public two-line-element catalogue fetched from CelesTrak (GROUP=stations, 21 distinct objects after keeping duplicate element sets in) via orbitguard.adapters.tle.Sgp4Propagator; conjunction screening and co-orbital partitioning via orbitguard.conjunction.find_tca and orbitguard.adapters.tle.partition_co_orbital over all C(21,2)=210 pairs, 24h window, 120s coarse step, reference epoch 2026-08-15T14:22:16.509423+00:00. This is a live public catalogue fetch, not a bundled/cached snapshot -- CelesTrak's data changes as TLEs are updated, so re-running the command below will fetch the current catalogue and may return different object positions and pair counts; the threshold/filter relationship shown here is what is stable, not the exact numbers.",
    "command": "cd flagship/orbitguard-twin && PYTHONPATH=src python scripts/real_screening.py --group stations --hours 24 --max-objects 60 --no-dedupe --out artifacts/stations.json",
    "generated": "2026-08-15",
    "measured": true
  }
